<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<TcPlcObject Version="1.1.0.1" ProductVersion="3.1.4026.18">
  <POU Name="_FC_GetVersionSynVisu" Id="{4d6b2f07-b33f-4006-af5c-24d1c8cfb62c}" SpecialFunc="None">
    <Declaration><![CDATA[(****************************************************************************************************<br>
© Syntegon Group.<br>
All rights reserved, also regarding any disposal, exploitation, reproduction, editing, distribution,<br>
as well as in the event of applications for industrial property rights.<br>
*****************************************************************************************************<br>
DESCRIPTION:<br>
Runtime-readable version of the Syn_Visu library.<br>
*****************************************************************************************************<br>
VERSION         ¦ DATE       ¦ NAME      ¦ CHANGE<br>
Syn_Visu 3.0.0  ¦ 2026-10-31 ¦ J.Willner ¦ Naming and layout after the TCAT programming guideline<br>
Syn_Visu 3.1.0  ¦ 2026-10-31 ¦ J.Willner ¦ Faults of components and XTS movers (protocol 8)<br>
Syn_Visu 3.2.0  ¦ 2026-10-31 ¦ J.Willner ¦ _FB_VisuConveyor.m_MoveProduct<br>
Syn_Visu 3.3.0  ¦ 2026-10-31 ¦ J.Willner ¦ Zone CCS offset, origin shift per component (protocol 9)<br>
Syn_Visu 3.4.0  ¦ 2026-11-01 ¦ J.Willner ¦ m_LatchProduct: product state and robot (PLACED onto outfeeds)<br>
Syn_Visu 3.5.0  ¦ 2026-11-01 ¦ J.Willner ¦ Product shapes: box, cylinder, rounded box (protocol 10)<br>
Syn_Visu 4.0.0  ¦ 2026-11-01 ¦ J.Willner ¦ Vision system, product sensor, zones without kind (protocol 11)<br>
Syn_Visu 5.0.0  ¦ 2026-11-01 ¦ J.Willner ¦ XTS tracks of track modules, a fault per module (protocol 12)<br>
Syn_Visu 5.1.0  ¦ 2026-11-01 ¦ J.Willner ¦ Manifest sLibraryVersion: the visualisation shows the library version<br>
Syn_Visu 6.0.0  ¦ 2026-11-01 ¦ J.Willner ¦ Generic product client (nLastClientId, ePreviousState), station (protocol 13)<br>
Syn_Visu 7.0.0  ¦ 2026-11-02 ¦ J.Willner ¦ Product poses in the conveyor's coordinate system (protocol 14)<br>
Syn_Visu 7.1.0  ¦ 2026-11-05 ¦ J.Willner ¦ VISU_un_MAX_PRODUCTS 4800: registers for machines with thousands of products<br>
Syn_Visu 7.2.0  ¦ 2026-11-05 ¦ J.Willner ¦ Conveyor: product index by id, registers rearranged with MEMMOVE<br>
Syn_Visu 8.0.0  ¦ 2026-11-05 ¦ J.Willner ¦ m_Register without vi_str_Path: the symbol path comes from the instance path<br>
Syn_Visu 8.0.0  ¦ 2026-11-05 ¦ J.Willner ¦ Methods without default values: every call lists all inputs (TwinCAT 4024)<br>
Syn_Visu 9.0.0  ¦ 2026-11-05 ¦ J.Willner ¦ Zones bounded across the belt: m_SetZone vi_lr_StartY, vi_lr_EndY (protocol 15)<br>
Syn_Visu 9.1.0  ¦ 2026-11-07 ¦ J.Willner ¦ Conveyor without a body: _FB_VisuConveyor.m_SetBodyVisible (protocol 16)<br>
Syn_Visu 9.2.0  ¦ 2026-11-07 ¦ J.Willner ¦ Cartesian robot without Y or Z axis: _FB_VisuCartesian.m_SetKinematics (protocol 17)<br>
Syn_Visu 9.3.0  ¦ 2026-11-07 ¦ J.Willner ¦ Limit area for XTS gantry and Cartesian: _FB_VisuRobot.m_SetLimitArea (protocol 18)<br>
Syn_Visu 9.4.0  ¦ 2026-11-09 ¦ J.Willner ¦ TCP limit area: _FB_VisuRobot.m_SetTcpLimitArea (protocol 19)<br>
Syn_Visu 9.5.0  ¦ 2026-11-11 ¦ J.Willner ¦ Finger offsets: m_SetFingerOffset, bPoseReported (protocol 20)<br>
Syn_Visu 9.6.0  ¦ 2026-11-12 ¦ J.Willner ¦ Product marks: m_SetProductMark, _FC_VisuSetMarkName (protocol 21)<br>
Syn_Visu 9.7.0  ¦ 2026-11-13 ¦ J.Willner ¦ Machine entry: _FB_VisuMachine, run state, machine messages (protocol 22)<br>
Syn_Visu 10.0.0 ¦ 2026-11-14 ¦ J.Willner ¦ Pose by m_SetPose, not m_Configure; m_McsToBelt, m_BeltToMcs<br>
****************************************************************************************************)
FUNCTION _FC_GetVersionSynVisu : UINT
VAR_INPUT
	vi_n_VersionElement					: INT;	// [-] 1 = major, 2 = minor, 3 = revision
END_VAR]]></Declaration>
    <Implementation>
      <ST><![CDATA[CASE vi_n_VersionElement OF
	1: _FC_GetVersionSynVisu := 10;
	2: _FC_GetVersionSynVisu := 0;
	3: _FC_GetVersionSynVisu := 0;
ELSE
	_FC_GetVersionSynVisu := 16#FFFF;
END_CASE]]></ST>
    </Implementation>
  </POU>
</TcPlcObject>